  "body": "The microARC 4 indexing in the PathPilot post (#785, PR #798) lifts Z to the top of travel (`G53 G0 Z0`) before every `G0 A..`, and that is the only clearance it gives. Nothing checks that the tool tip (and holder) at that Z clears the radius swept by the part, the chuck and its jaws while A turns. On the 3/4\" test bar it does with room to spare; a larger part, a larger chuck or a long tool could hit while the table turns. Today the tester-kit README asks the operator to confirm it by hand.\n\nA `G30` before every tool change also moves A to the stored G30 position (LinuxCNC params 5181-5189) with Z already at the top, which is the same check at another A.\n\nDone means: before an A index (and wherever the program can turn A), the program gate or the simulation compares the swept radius of the stock/part and the stated chuck against the tool tip and holder at the post's safe Z, and refuses by name, naming the operation and the clearance short, when they can meet. Pinned by a test with a part that clears and one that does not.\n\nPart of #785\n",
